        "page": 8,
        "text": "▪ Equivalent units is a derived amount of output units that takes the quantity of each input in units completed or in work in progress and converts it into the amount of completed output units that could be made with the quantity of input. ▪ Put differently: It is a way to measure how much work has been done on partially completed products as if they were fully finished. 28.04.2026 Benjamin Falch 10 Equivalent Units (BHDR, 2023, po. 94-95) A factory manufactures chairs: - 100 chairs, 100% finished - 50 chairs, 50% finished (they have the frame but no legs or cushions) - 20 chairs, 25% finished (just the frame started) Calculation of EU: Finished chairs: 100 EU 50% complete chairs: 50*50% = 25 EU 25% complete chairs: 20*25% = 5 EU 130 EU 170 chairs started Interpretation: This means the workers have done the same amount of work as if they had finished 130 chairs."
