        "sessionTitle": "Budgeting & Variance Analysis",
        "page": 3,
        "text": "a) Drawing on exhibit 14.3 (BHDR, p. 430), explain the sequence of steps in preparing a master budget. 08.01.2026 Benjamin Falch 5 Exercise 5.2 Definition of a budget: “A budget is a quantitative expression of a proposed plan of action by management for a future time period and is an aid to the coordination and implementation of the plan” (BHDR, 2023, p. 423). The masterbudget is a comprehensive financial plan that integrates all of a company’s individual budgets into a unified document. Operating decisions are about the acquisition and use of scarce resources. Financing decisions deal with how to obtain the funds to acquire resources (BHDR, 2023, p. 423)."
