        "session": 5,
        "sessionTitle": "Budgeting & Variance Analysis",
        "page": 4,
        "text": "a) Drawing on exhibit 14.3 (BHDR, p. 430), explain the sequence of steps in preparing a master budget. 08.01.2026 Benjamin Falch 6 Exercise 5.2 (1) Sales budget • Foundation of the master budget • It forecasts the expected sales volume and revenue • Factors considered: market demand, historical sales trends, pricing strategies, etc. • Production depends on the forecast level of revenue! (2) Production budget • Based on the sales forecast, this budget determines the number of units that need to be produced (3) Direct materials & labour budget • Quantity and costs of raw material required for production • Estimation of direct labour hours & costs required for production"
